sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant A as Transaction A
  participant L as Room advisory lock
  participant DB as bookings + GiST index
  participant B as Transaction B

  Note over A,B: Both want Nilgiri 10:00–11:00 at the same instant (READ COMMITTED)
  A->>L: pg_advisory_xact_lock(Nilgiri) → granted
  B->>L: pg_advisory_xact_lock(Nilgiri) → WAITS
  A->>DB: insert row + index entry, check overlaps → none
  A->>A: COMMIT (lock released)
  L-->>B: lock granted
  B->>DB: insert row + index entry, check overlaps
  DB-->>B: finds A's committed row → ERROR 23P01
  B->>B: ROLLBACK → API answers 409
  Note over A,B: Had A rolled back instead, B's check would find nothing and B would succeed
  Note over A,B: Without the advisory lock, B would wait on A's uncommitted index entry instead: same outcome, but several simultaneous writers could wait on each other (deadlock → 40P01 → retry)
